{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming","id":1190942,"title":"Of Firstborns Less Told [Brainstorming]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-02T04:39:45-08:00","id":1190942,"title":"Of Firstborns Less Told [Brainstorming]","content":"Everyone know the names of Father Wolf's greatest children, as each of them acts as a patron of one of the People's Tribes- Destroyer Wolf, Death Wolf, Black Wolf, Red Wolf and Winter Wolf; Rabid Wolf, Silver Wolf and Dire Wolf. Five on the side of the Forsaken, three on the side of the Pure, eight overall. However, what most of the modern Uratha don't know is that those Firstborn, while being the greatest, were not the only ones. Other Firstborn have lurked the wilderness of Pangaea in the ancient days, hunting either alongside their siblings or on their own. With the fall of the Predator Paradise, some of those Firstborn have fallen to sleep. Others have died, just like their Father. Others have found solace in the furthermost reaches of Hisil or other realms unknown, and few have suffered from even stranger, weirder fates. This thread is for those Firstborn, both lost and found, so their story could be told- and by telling their story, they would become true.<br /> <br /> In short, in here I'm going to list all of the &quot;bastard children&quot; of Father Wolf which have not established a Tribe of their own, and some thoughts about what such tribe would be. Adding new, homebrew Firstborn is more than welcomed, and feel free to add your thoughts about the subject :P<br /> <br /> Soulless Wolf- the most famous of the &quot;unknown Firstborn&quot;, Viruhk- Ur is the secret shame of the family. While there are many versions for his existence, I personally prefer the &quot;fallen Firstborn&quot; version, with him serving as the power which units the many Maeljin cults and lodges of the Bale Hounds together. Being a Firstborn who fell to Inferno's clutches, he is undoubtedly one of the most dangerous spirit lords out there. Perhaps once his chosen prey were demons, and like any other Firstborn, he adjusted himself to be more like his prey to hunt them better.. until he took one step too far, and fell to the abyss from which he can no longer be reclaimed (like what may have happened if Black Wolf would have shattered her Omphalos Stone). Or maybe, it is just a trick- maybe Soulless Wolf is still loyal to his hunt, and he simply works to feel the Maeljin themselves- he seemingly support their cause, yet behind the scenes work to downplay the influence of the Bale Hounds and teaches under cover the secrets of the Wounds for potential demon hunters. It takes a demon to fight a demon, after all- and one day, when Virukh- Ur's true Tribe would rise among the ranks of the Bale Hounds, the Asah Gadar would be shattered for once and for all.<br /> <br /> Watcher Wolf- being presented in the Rage, Udzhalla- Ur is presented as a potential totem of the &quot;secret police&quot; Tribe (the Tower Hounds). While some parts may be adjusted (as the Blood Talons cover some bits of the concept), she could undoubtedly still be around. For some reason, it feels more naturally in my eyes for her and her Tribe to side with the Pure than with the Forsaken, as their Sacred Hunt feels to be focused less around a certain breed and more ideologically bent, like the Fire Touched target lairs and the Ivory Claws hunt for those of tainted lineage (I think?).<br /> <br /> Growling Wolf- another of the optional Tribe patrons, Ramammu- Ur patrons a Tribe of diplomats called the Speakers of the Vine. In general, the Firstborn feels like the one who would prefer to not choose sides, as he tries to negotiate between them. I kinda wonder about what prey he may have, as once more he feels more focused around a concept than a supernatural breed- a political hunt of some kind. Perhaps his prey is &quot;kings&quot;, or something of that concept? You know, leaders of some kind, something which would focus around a political hunt.<br /> <br /> Ravening Wolf- being introduced in the Pack, Isim- Ur was dead for a long, long, long, loooooooong time, before she was revived in the wilds of Mongolia. Under her guidance, the Eaters of the Dead were established, and it has started to hunt her ancient prey- the dead, and the undead. As she returns to her former strength, the Lodge may become a Tribe, and the chances are the Forsaken would gladly accept her help (even if the Iron Masters would frown a little bit, as currently vampires are under their Hunt).<br /> <br /> Eater of Names- a mystery wrapped in enigma, the Eater of Names has been introduced in the Sundered World, and has drawn more and more attention since then. Focused around mages and other occultists as her favored prey, she has been mentioned by our dear old Chris Allen more than once. She may be active in Hong Kong, if to believe the title of Chris's actual play, and may be responsible to the mysterious force which devours the Change of young Uratha (I think, I need to check the original thread). She also seems to have some symbiotic relationship with Death Wolf- for as the one search for wisdom, the other devours it.<br /> <br /> Sky Hunter- nothing more than a sentence, Sky Hunter is mentioned as one of the greatest hunters of the Firstborn, just next to Dire Wolf and Destroyer Wolf. Heck, they are described as being &quot;terrible&quot; in that sentence. That makes me think that Sky Hunter may be truly a terrifying sight to behold, a monster capable of mass destruction like the other two. As a &quot;Sky Hunter&quot;, I assume that they focus their efforts around flying monsters of some kind, perhaps with things like the Distant Ones, or maybe anyone who dares to cross the heavens, no matter if it comes from above or bellow. From planes and aircraft to invading spirits from the Outer Space, Sky Hunter attacks anything which dares to cross the firmament. With its &quot;windy&quot; elemental nature, they may be a good patrons to the Savage Priests suggested in the Rage, even if they'll need some rework to different them from the Fire Touched.<br /> <br /> Whisperer Wolf- or Wolf Who Whispers, is another lesser known member of the Firstborn from Dark Eras. There is nothing told about them other than the fact that they aren't really famous and are of limited nature, such as Black Wolf. Sure, Mother Wolf may be an important figure now, but apparently the Hosts were not seen as much of a threat back than, and the Sacred Places didn't need a lot of protection. As having &quot;whispers&quot; as a theme, I wonder if they could perhaps be better totems for the Savage Priests, as they do seem to have some mystical nature. With Death Wolf focusing around the spirit worlds, and the Eater of Names being based around mages, I wonder what niche would Whisperer have- perhaps she could be focused around the God Machine and its angels, as she works against the heaven presented by the Machine's cold logic?<br /> <br /> Opalescent- one part of the Twins, they are mentioned to rise &quot;whole clans&quot; of man and wolf in the name of Warden Moon. While they are undoubtedly connected to Luna much more than the rest of the Uratha, I wonder what kind of prey they could have. Perhaps as they serve as &quot;those enlightened by another&quot;, they would hunt for sources of light? Celestial spirits, perhaps? I do tend to lean them toward being Artemis as their twin is Apollo, I think that Black Wolf has already the &quot;virgin huntress&quot; theme going for her. Perhaps, on the other hand, we have already met Opalescent. After all, there is already one silver coated Wolf among the Firstborn, and while he has a different name, it is not uncommon for the Firstborn to change their name with a change of their nature (such as Seeking Wolf becoming Death Wolf, or Creation Wolf turning into Rabid Wolf).<br /> <br /> Incandescent- the other twin, Incandescent is to the sun what Opalescent is to the moon. Considering we are talking about a sun-aligned, golden wolf, we already have such a spirit lord in the canon, one who is actually said to serve as the totem of a Lodge which claims neutrality between the Forsaken and the Pure, and that has an Omphalos Stone- Apollo the Sun Wolf. Again, a change of name means a change of nature, and as it seems Sun Wolf may have truly changed through the years, after he was banished to the reaches of the sun for being more of a Void spirit than anything else. While Incandescent seems much friendlier than Apollo, who knows why the Firstborn was banished in the first place, and how the fall of Pangaea has influenced him?<br /> <br /> Well, that's what I got for now. I may think about a few homebrew Firstborn later. Feel free to detail your thoughts about the subject :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T04:48:16-08:00","id":1190944,"title":"","content":"There's also Secondborn, the offspring of Urfarah's Firstborn. Unlike them, Secondborn could arise at any time, and a conflict like a titanomachie seems fitting. What sort of thing could spring from Fenris or Kamduis-Ur? Or even Husuruth-Ur?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T04:54:59-08:00","id":1190947,"title":"","content":"What book are the second born from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T05:28:21-08:00","id":1190951,"title":"","content":"They're mentioned in The Rage: Forsaken's Player Guide (1e)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T08:05:45-08:00","id":1190980,"title":"","content":"They're also in some other books, Garm is probably the most well-known Secondborn. But there's also Ankakumikaityn the Nomad Wolf, child of Dire Wolf, who is the totem of the lodge of swords.<br /> <br /> Lodges the Faithful gets into it, and how some powerful spirits might lie about being Secondborn. In the book there's a likely example, as the Lodge of the Feast, a Bale Hound Lodge, has a 'Ravening Wolf' as a totem that is theorized by some to be an aspect of Baalphegor, the King of Gluttony.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Firstborn, I imagine there's some water-based one to match the Sky Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T08:10:35-08:00","id":1190983,"title":"","content":"Heh, The Salty Sea Dog","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T09:45:26-08:00","id":1191017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1190980#post1190980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding the Firstborn, I imagine there's some water-based one to match the Sky Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something in the style of the &quot;Wave Rider&quot; (that is, a Firstborn focused around the upper level of the sea, like storms and beaches), or &quot;Darkness Beneath the Waves&quot; (which cares more for the horrors in the depths of the ocean)? I assume that both versions could be combined into one, as Sea and her spawn was one of the greatest threats of the Pangaean world, and it would make a Tribe of sailors and explorers which guard against the horrors that hide in the depths of the abyss? (no, not that Abyss.. I think).<br /> <br /> Also, some thoughts about homebrew Firstborn-<br /> <br /> - a Firstborn focused around hunting ancient artifacts of old, which would probably put it at odds with the Arisen, Sin Eaters, the AKD and other people with strong attachment for their objects. &quot;Collector Wolf&quot; sounds a bit awkward, but I think that &quot;Buried Wolf&quot; sounds cool.<br /> <br /> - Dream Wolf, which hunts after beings from the Astral, and perhaps even horrors of the Primordial Dream. <br /> <br /> - a Firstborn which hunts for other shapeshifters, such as the Baal Hadad or the Changing Breeds. I think that &quot;Wearer of Skins&quot; could be a nice name for it.<br /> <br /> - Hedge Wolf, which search for anything fey, may be nice (no, I'm not calling them &quot;Big Bad Wolf&quot;).<br /> <br /> - a Firstborn which hunts after abyssal entities (unless it would fall into Wave Rider's alley)<br /> <br /> - Inspiration Wolf, of course! They hunt after the best ideas and bring them to to writers who they deem worthy :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T10:35:54-08:00","id":1191035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1191017#post1191017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Hedge Wolf, which search for anything fey, may be nice (no, I'm not calling them &quot;Big Bad Wolf&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about missed opportunities, the go-to name for a Changeling-crossover Firstborn would be <i>Briar Wolf</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T10:55:45-08:00","id":1191041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1191035#post1191035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking about missed opportunities, the go-to name for a Changeling-crossover Firstborn would be <i>Briar Wolf</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Br'er Wolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T11:22:50-08:00","id":1191059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1191017#post1191017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- a Firstborn focused around hunting ancient artifacts of old, which would probably put it at odds with the Arisen, Sin Eaters, the AKD and other people with strong attachment for their objects. &quot;Collector Wolf&quot; sounds a bit awkward, but I think that &quot;Buried Wolf&quot; sounds cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glitter Wolf? The Taker of Things? Might be able to tie this into the Maeljin of Greed or Envy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - a Firstborn which hunts for other shapeshifters, such as the Baal Hadad or the Changing Breeds. I think that &quot;Wearer of Skins&quot; could be a nice name for it. </div> </div> </div>This might actually work as a second edition version of Scavenger Wolf, from Skinchangers. It might even be the progenitor of skinchangers, having been a Pangaean Firstborn that became a human to avoid the fate of other Pangaeans and, from there, anything else. It could fit more for Envy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - a Firstborn which hunts after abyssal entities (unless it would fall into Wave Rider's alley) </div> </div> </div>I believe there's a Dreaming Wolf mentioned in the Australia Hunting Ground but it might fit here too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-02-2018, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T12:06:50-08:00","id":1191069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1191041#post1191041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about Br'er Wolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>You and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> are precious. Both are delightful and likely alternate names for the same entity. I really can't see how the Firstborn would miss out on Arcadia, even as it would be <i>very strange </i>to them. (Do spirits, even Pangaeans, dream?)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T12:39:57-08:00","id":1191085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1191069#post1191069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> are precious. Both are delightful and likely alternate names for the same entity. I really can't see how the Firstborn would miss out on Arcadia, even as it would be <i>very strange </i>to them. (Do spirits, even Pangaeans, dream?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Pangaeans can meditate themselves into the Temenos and Anima Mundi. And there's a lot of spirits associated with dreams, like the Omen Grinder and Luna herself, who shares them with the Cahalith. We even had some simple Dream Manipulation mechanics in first edition.<br /> <br /> That said, if something exists, or even doesn't exist, there's likely something that can hunt it. One can wake from any dream, and every story has an Ending, after all. I've been leaning towards considering the True Fae as a host, if only due to their mention of being a stereotype in the Hunters in Darkness section, perhaps from some original Dream or Tale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:20:56-08:00","id":1191122,"title":"","content":"How are they like hosts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:23:33-08:00","id":1191124,"title":"","content":"They are smaller parts of a larger whole, take each others titles, parasitize aspects of the world while also having effect on a Gauntlet equivalent, with the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:42:37-08:00","id":1191130,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t forget they can spread and effect changing. Also werewolves hunting true fae that would be a interesting story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T14:58:43-08:00","id":1191138,"title":"","content":"A proper Changeling/Werewolf crossover story is on my someday-eventually list of things to do. Back when freeholds were supposed to have bulwarks, I wanted to see the Siskur-Dah used for one and started building a Lodge around the concept, but I never got far enough along to write anything down. I'd love to see someone take a shot at such a crossover setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T03:43:14-08:00","id":1193870,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts about how to divide the potential tribes of the &quot;lesser Firstborn&quot; among the factions of the People-<br /> <br /> Soulless Wolf- as the patron of the Bale Hounds, he stands on his own. If he works behind the scenes to train an &quot;exorcist tribe&quot;, however, I think he could fall to the Forsaken's alley, even if on its furthermost edge, with them having infernals as their &quot;sacred prey&quot;, and serves as the totem of a &quot;tribe of exorcists&quot;<br /> <br /> Watcher Wolf- seems to be more of a Pure material than a Forsaken one, with her having &quot;those who dishonor the law&quot; as her sacred prey, and with her serving as the totem of a &quot;tribe of secret police&quot;<br /> <br /> Growling Wolf- still kinda struggling with him. I tend to align him with the Pure, but I still tries to think what kind of prey would the &quot;tribe of diplomats&quot; would hunt. Maybe &quot;those who dishonor society&quot;? Or &quot;those who dishonor resources&quot;? Sure, it would make them a bit nicer than the rest of the Pure, but it makes sense for them to take a more neutral position in relation to the Forsaken, at least on the outside.<br /> <br /> Ravening Wolf- with her even the dead as her sacred prey, it feels like she has a solid place among the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Eater of Names- I think she could work nicely as a Forsaken totem, with occultists as her prey, but I feel like there has to be something a bit more.. insidious about her. Her tribe would be censures of some kind, I assume, who hide/destroy forbidden lore and heretic rites, while utilizing them to their own benefit. Some kind of &quot;church warlocks&quot;, I think. Perhaps they would end up on a neutral ground, together with Soulless and Growling Wolves.<br /> <br /> Sky Hunter- while at first I thought about him as a Forsaken totem, I think he could work better as a member of the Pure, having &quot;those who dishonor the boundaries&quot;. I could see his acting as a totem for a tribe of gatekeepers and stormwardens of some kind.<br /> <br /> Wolf Who Whispers- after giving it some thought, I think she would work the best as the &quot;abyssal Firstborn&quot;, which would make her either as Forsaken or as a neutral tribe totem. For the tribe itself, I think they would be a &quot;tribe of philosophers&quot;, who search to find the truth in the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Opalescent- I'm still pretty sure that's the old name for Silver Wolf, before something bad happened to his twin.<br /> <br /> Incandescent- as Apollo Wolf, we know that his prey is &quot;those who dishonor the temples of the sun&quot;, which is kinda Pure-y. As the Temple choose a neutral stand, it makes sense for the tribe version to stay neutral, similarly to the other &quot;Ghost Wolf Tribes&quot;, or join the Pure.<br /> <br /> Sea Wolf- as the hunter of the horrors of the sea (or perhaps Sea? She was a terror during Pangaea, after all. It makes sense to have a Firstborn dedicated to hunt her spawn), it feels to me that she would work better as a Forsaken tribe. I assume her tribe would be the &quot;tribe of explorers&quot; detailed in the Rage, and we could tie her to the Drowned from Shadows of UK (with them being a part of her prey).<br /> <br /> Glitter Wolf- I think he could work as a Pure totem, hunting for &quot;those who dishonor the relics of the past&quot;. I assume he would have a &quot;tribe of temple guardians&quot; in his service.<br /> <br /> Dreaming Wolf- with her hunting for dreams and nightmares, I think she would work well as a part of the Forsaken, acting as a totem for a &quot;tribe of visionaries&quot;. Could be tied to the Dreaming Lodge, as suggested.<br /> <br /> Wearer of Skins- with focus around other shapeshifters (or &quot;Luna's bastards&quot;), I could see him working as a Forsaken totem. On the other hand, perhaps taking a neutral stance would work better for his &quot;tribe of survivors&quot;.<br /> <br /> Briar Wolf- as a Firstborn hunting for the fey and Arcadia, I think she would definitely be Forsaken. Her tribe would probably be a &quot;tribe of bards and storytellers&quot;, I think.<br /> <br /> Night Wolf- the God Machine dedicated Firstborn (I'm assuming that the Field of Dogs would be either absorbed or destroyed by the Eaters of the Dead), he would hunt for false idols and angels of the Machine. Would work nicely as the patron of the &quot;tribe of priests&quot; presented in the Rage. I tend to put them on the Pure side (as &quot;those who disrespect the faith&quot;), but as they already have their own priests I think they would be better as a Forsaken tribe.<br /> <br /> So, to sum things up (and by including existing tribes), we would potentially have 10 Forsaken Tribes, 6 Pure Tribes and 6 Ghost Tribes (all is subject to be changed, of course). I assume, of course, that the &quot;Ghost Tribes&quot; would have much less numbers than the Forsaken/Pure. Next step- to start thinking about cool names for the tribes (of course, if someone has a cool concept for more Firstborns feel free to pitch in, or comment about the Forsaken/Pure/Ghost division).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T10:41:50-08:00","id":1193974,"title":"","content":"Curious why you think Briar Wolf would be Forsaken? The real moon doesn't seem to be in the Hedge or Arcadia, it would be perfect for Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T10:59:30-08:00","id":1193981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1193974#post1193974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious why you think Briar Wolf would be Forsaken? The real moon doesn't seem to be in the Hedge or Arcadia, it would be perfect for Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I practically divided them according to the prey they hunt- those who hunt for a certain &quot;breed&quot; are Forsaken, while those who hunt for a &quot;condition&quot; (meaning, those who dishonor &quot;x&quot;) are Pure. As faeries are an actual breed of monsters, slotting them to the Forsaken made sense. They may work better for a neutral tribe, on the other hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T10:59:55-07:00","id":1195378,"title":"","content":"So some thoughts about the Tribes themselves-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Ghost Tribes</u></b><br /> Soulless Wolf (following the &quot;inside tribe&quot; option)- Howlers of Hell, tribe of exorcists and hunters of demons. Renown: Cunning. Gifts: Warding, Knowledge, Dominance (potentially replacing one of the with a an homebrew Gift of Wounds)<br /> <br /> Growling Wolf- Speakers of the Vine, tribe of diplomats and hunters of those who dishonor their people. Primary Renown: Purity. Secondary Renown: Cunning and Wisdom. Gifts: Insight, Inspiration, Dominance, Nature. Skills: Politics, Empathy, Persuasion.<br /> <br /> Eater of Names- Devoured Letters, tribe of censures and hunters of occultists. Renown: Wisdom. Gifts: Knowledge, Insight, Warding (potentially replacing one of the options with an homebrew Gift of Oblivion)<br /> <br /> Wolf Who Whispers- Void Binders, tribe of philosophers and hunters of the Abyss. Renown: Wisdom. Gifts: Insight, Warding, Shaping<br /> <br /> Sun Wolf- Temple of Apollo, tribe of wardens and hunters of those who dishonor the temples. Primary Renown: Purity. Secondary Renown: Wisdom, Glory. Gifts: Elemental, Inspiration, Dominance, Warding (potentially replacing one of the options with an homebrew Gift of Radiance). Skills: Occult, Socialize, Medicine<br /> <br /> Scavenger Wolf- Skinner Beasts, tribe of survivors and hunters of shapeshifters. Renown: Cunning. Gifts: Nature, Shaping, Strength<br /> <br /> Briar Wolf- Fey Dogs, tribe of bards and hunters of goblins. Renown: Glory. Gifts: Rage, Shaping, Insight (potentially replacing one of the options with an homebrew Gift of Song).<br /> <br /> Roaming Wolf- Dust Walkers, tribe of nomads and hunters of the created. Renown: Wisdom. Gifts: Elemental, Stealth, Knowledge<br /> <br /> Blood Wolf- Avenging Brethren, tribe of zealots and hunters of those who disrespect the hunters. Renown: Purity. Gifts: Rage, Warding, Larceny<br /> <br /> <b><u>Pure Tribes</u></b><br /> Watcher Wolf- Tower Hounds, tribe of spies and hunters of those who dishonor the law. Primary Renown: Honor. Secondary Renown: Purity and Cunning. Gifts: Warding, Stealth, Evasion, Insight. Skills: Larceny, Investigation, Subterfuge<br /> <br /> Sky Hunter- Horizon Watchers, tribe of gatekeepers and hunters of those who dishonor the boundaries. Primary Renown: Glory. Secondary Renown: Honor and Cunning. Gifts: Weather, Warding, Strength. Skills: Survival, Athletics, Intimidation<br /> <br /> Glitter Wolf- Collectors of the Lost, tribe of archivists and hunters of those who dishonor the past. Primary Renown: Wisdom. Secondary Renown: Cunning, Glory. Gifts: Warding, Shaping, Knowledge, Stealth. Skills: Occult, Investigation, Academics.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Forsaken Tribes</u></b><br /> Ravening Wolf- Eaters of the Dead, tribe of cleaners and hunters of the undead. Renown: Purity. Gifts: Death, Strength, Warding<br /> <br /> Sea Wolf- Wave Riders, tribe of mariners and hunters of the drowned. Renown: Glory. Gifts: Weather, Elemental, Strength (potentially replacing one of the options with an homebrew Gift of Seas)<br /> <br /> Dreaming Wolf- Sleeping Seers, tribe of visionaries and hunters of goetia. Renown: Wisdom. Gifts: Inspiration, Shaping, Evasion (potentially replacing one of the options with an homebrew Gift of Dreams)<br /> <br /> Night Wolf- Savage Priests, tribe of clerics and hunters of angels. Renown: Glory. Gifts: Dominance, Strength, Technology<br /> <br /> Burrow Wolf- Lantern Bearers, tribe of redeemers and hunters of the underfolk. Renown: Purity. Gifts: Rage, Stealth, Warding<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, those are the pitches I have for now. I'll think about bans and Sacred Hunts later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 04-23-2018, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:22:04-07:00","id":1196470,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts about origin stories for three of our Firstborn:<br /> <br /> Soulless Wolf- Pangaea has died with Father Wolf's last howl. Silent Wolf, an outside to his family, recognized it- but his job was not over yet. In fact, it has only just began- for without the Great Predator to tend the Shadow, corruption has took hold, and its roots reached deep. Hisil was wounded, over and over again, and dark spirits which until than were held in bay has feasted upon the chaos and terror and grew in power. Recognizing that there was no way for him to remove the corruption which has started to fester, Silent Wolf came before the Lord of the Wound and pledge allegiance. If you can't beat them, join them- that's what he said. Gleeful for the chance to corrupt such a mighty spirit, the Maeljin accepted the former demon hunter and taught him the ways of vice, granting him the name of Soulless Wolf and a betrayer of his own family. At least, that's how it seemed- for hidden from all, Soulless Wolf hid a single shard of his heart, so it would remain pure and true to its cause- the only way he could infiltrate the heart of the darkness and not be devoured. Since than, Soulless Wolf has served as the Eyes of the Maeljin and patron of the Bale Hounds- but he kept at least one eye open for those who were willing to learn the paths of Hell without being corrupted, and fight the demons with their own tools. Before those, he manifested as his true, untainted self- giving them gifts and secrets unknown by all, and one command. Stay silent, until the time to strike would come. Soon, Hell would taste its own medicine.<br /> <br /> Growling Wolf- one of the youngest of the Firstborn, Growling Wolf has never had much interest in the hunt, always being one more interested in talking than fighting (his mother's fault, if Red Wolf were to be asked). As such, none of his older siblings took him seriously, leaving him alone to speak with the cults of man and deal with the politics of the Shadow. Only Creation Wolf had a soft spot for him, and even as she was consumed by plague Growling Wolf stuck with her, uncaring for the changes which passed upon the world. Having little to no interest in the Uratha society, he stayed mostly away from the dispute of the Tribes, serving merely as a patron to the small Lodge of Mania (which he found to be hilarious)- but every once in ten years, he and Rabid Wolf met, discussing spirituality and philosophy, and the opinions of man and spirit. For ages the meetings were kept intact- until in the last one, as he came to meet his sister, he discovered she was not alone- his brothers, Dire Wolf and Silver Wolf, has accompanied her to the meeting. Scolding their sibling, they told him that they waited long enough, and it was the time for him to &quot;grow up&quot; and &quot;stop shaming their father's memory&quot;. Seeing no other choice, Growling Wolf accepted the ultimatum (for he, like any other sane being, did not wanted to be on Dire Wolf's bad side, for he probably was light-years from &quot;sane&quot;). Revealing himself before those Pure who ripped their Auspice yet chose no tribe, Growling Wolf provided a worthy challenge for those whom he deemed worthy- to hunt with no claw or fang, no tooth or nail. Those who succeeded have became the first of his Tribe, hunters of word and letter. Yet, even in his situation Growling Wolf wasn't able to fully commit himself to the struggle- making him and his followers at the outskirts of the Pure society, and serving as a bridge between the two, conflicting sides.<br /> <br /> Night Wolf- a child of faith, Night Wolf has always searched for a meaning higher of his own, something which was above the wild and untamed chaos of the Shadow. He roamed the Bordered Marches of Pangaea, searched heaven and earth in an attempt to find something more, something higher and greater. Thinking it was just a phase, his siblings left him for his own hunts- for as long as he didn't disturb anyone, what kind of damage such a hopeless search would have? And yet, during one, moonless night, Night Wolf did the impossible- he found something, a god of metal and steam, a machine which held purpose for any being upon the face of earth. Fascinated by divine machinery, Night Wolf felt humility and bowed before the idol, pledging loyalty knowing that his hunt was over once and forever. The machine has accepted the offer- and than, his nightmare has only started. Trapped by its mechanical clutches, the machine has swallowed Night Wolf whole- and with the fall of Pangaea his siblings has barely even noticed, and those who did believed he died with the Gauntlet's collapse. Yet, Night Wolf lived still- his body and heart being violated by the divine creation, transformed and probed and tormented again and again, until the day his god decided he was ready to serve him. Giving him the name of Lycaon, he served as a totem to a cannibal lodge which served to power the idol through human sacrifice, growing in power with each and every day. Bound by machinery, Lycaon was perfectly faith to the machine and served its mission- until the day another Firstborn thought to be long dead challenged his control, and rose against his faithful with a lodge of his own. Long as raging was the battle between the two godlings, until the faithful of Ravening Wolf has found the heart of Lycaon bound by foreign machinery. Shattering the prison which contained his soul, Lycaon was freed from the bindings and transformation of his god, and returned to be Night Wolf once more. On that day, he made a new pledge to himself, and forced those of his Lodge who survived to take it with him- serve no false god, and hunt the cursed idol who claimed to be divine. Finally, Night Wolf found the meaning he was searching for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T01:17:48-07:00","id":1238818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1191017#post1191017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something in the style of the &amp;quot;Wave Rider&amp;quot; (that is, a Firstborn focused around the upper level of the sea, like storms and beaches), or &amp;quot;Darkness Beneath the Waves&amp;quot; (which cares more for the horrors in the depths of the ocean)? I assume that both versions could be combined into one, as Sea and her spawn was one of the greatest threats of the Pangaean world, and it would make a Tribe of sailors and explorers which guard against the horrors that hide in the depths of the abyss? (no, not that Abyss.. I think).<br /> <br /> Also, some thoughts about homebrew Firstborn-<br /> <br /> - a Firstborn focused around hunting ancient artifacts of old, which would probably put it at odds with the Arisen, Sin Eaters, the AKD and other people with strong attachment for their objects. &amp;quot;Collector Wolf&amp;quot; sounds a bit awkward, but I think that &amp;quot;Buried Wolf&amp;quot; sounds cool.<br /> <br /> - Dream Wolf, which hunts after beings from the Astral, and perhaps even horrors of the Primordial Dream. <br /> <br /> - a Firstborn which hunts for other shapeshifters, such as the Baal Hadad or the Changing Breeds. I think that &amp;quot;Wearer of Skins&amp;quot; could be a nice name for it.<br /> <br /> - Hedge Wolf, which search for anything fey, may be nice (no, I'm not calling them &amp;quot;Big Bad Wolf&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> - a Firstborn which hunts after abyssal entities (unless it would fall into Wave Rider's alley)<br /> <br /> - Inspiration Wolf, of course! They hunt after the best ideas and bring them to to writers who they deem worthy :P</div> </div> </div> </div>The Baal Hadad? What is that and where can I read about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T01:24:49-07:00","id":1238819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargrskol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1238818#post1238818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Baal Hadad? What is that and where can I read about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also called the <i>gudthabak</i>, they\u2019re bull-shifters. Detailed in War Against the Pure (1e book) as one of the alternate shapechangers. They \u2018reproduce\u2019 by magically turning Wolf-Blooded into them. In Dark Eras it\u2019s revealed they were originally created in the Neolithic era by, IIRC, exposure to the residual spirit energies of Bull the Pangaean\u2019s pieces of his horn (or was it the Omphalos?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T01:33:04-07:00","id":1238820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1238819#post1238819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also called the <i>gudthabak</i>, they\u2019re bull-shifters. Detailed in War Against the Pure (1e book) as one of the alternate shapechangers. They \u2018reproduce\u2019 by magically turning Wolf-Blooded into them. In Dark Eras it\u2019s revealed they were originally created in the Neolithic era by, IIRC, exposure to the residual spirit energies of Bull the Pangaean\u2019s pieces of his horn (or was it the Omphalos?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok wow so that just blew my mind a bit, I only asked cause I've thought that changing breeds were portrayed as very rare in the chronicles of darkness and there wasn't that much lore spread around for them to have hunters of any kind(but it also makes since for a story as well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T03:00:04-07:00","id":1238829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargrskol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1238820#post1238820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok wow so that just blew my mind a bit, I only asked cause I've thought that changing breeds were portrayed as very rare in the chronicles of darkness and there wasn't that much lore spread around for them to have hunters of any kind(but it also makes since for a story as well)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well technically, the Baal Hadad aren\u2019t Changing Breeds as the book defines them. So are the other four shapechangers in War Against the Pure - them and the Colony (cats), the Unclean (cockroaches), the Brineborn (fish), and the Distant Ones (falcons) are all unrelated to Ferals. But then again, Ferals themselves seem to count Uratha as their own, so from their POV the five shapechangers would be Ferals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T03:50:41-07:00","id":1238846,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t forget Scavenger Wolf!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T12:57:53-07:00","id":1256201,"title":"","content":"Been making some searches on Internet and seen this unknown Firstborn...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.facebook.com/chiarabautistaartwork/photos/a.558941394158718/1078442085541977/?type=3&amp;ifg=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://www.facebook.com/chiarabautistaartwork/photos/a.558941394158718/1078442085541977/?type=3&amp;ifg=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://scontent-waw1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/12643006_1078442085541977_8245637362508760587_n.jpg?_nc_cat=105&amp;oh=21d28d1222129a9ebc040a4c0c4a16cd&amp;oe=5C23F16C\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So what -- we have now Star Wolf? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T13:12:05-07:00","id":1256206,"title":"","content":"Star Wolf, you say?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/egamia/images/9/97/Wolf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/egamia/images/9/97/Wolf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/egamia/images/9/97/Wolf.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/egamia/images/9/97/Wolf.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T00:39:44-07:00","id":1256386,"title":"","content":"Let's just assume we have Star Wolf - and that she leads small Lodge-trying-to-become-Tribe - <i>Star-Gazers</i>. What would her Totem children by like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T02:18:26-07:00","id":1256406,"title":"","content":"Well, Apocalypse's Stargazers had a camp which fought against vampiric beings, and while hunting the dead is Ravening Wolf's territory, perhaps having vampires as sacred hunt would work for Star Wolf's chosen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T03:07:33-07:00","id":1256414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1256406#post1256406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Apocalypse's Stargazers had a camp which fought against vampiric beings, and while hunting the dead is Ravening Wolf's territory, perhaps having vampires as sacred hunt would work for Star Wolf's chosen?</div> </div> </div> </div>With wierd star spirits and Void Leviathans, I feel like just sticking to what W:tA did is a missed opportunity.<br /> <br /> Or for other prey, Things-That-Should-Not-Be (Second Sight) or Abyssals, what with the whole Stars Are Right theme many have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-22T10:28:21-07:00","id":1256505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1256201#post1256201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been making some searches on Internet and seen this unknown Firstborn...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-waw1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/12643006_1078442085541977_8245637362508760587_n.jpg?_nc_cat=105&amp;oh=21d28d1222129a9ebc040a4c0c4a16cd&amp;oe=5C23F16C\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So what -- we have now Star Wolf? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1256386#post1256386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's just assume we have Star Wolf - and that she leads small Lodge-trying-to-become-Tribe - <i>Star-Gazers</i>. What would her Totem children by like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1256414#post1256414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With wierd star spirits and Void Leviathans, I feel like just sticking to what W:tA did is a missed opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go with star spirits and Void Leviathans as Prey for Star Gazers! They could become cool fan addition to <i>Start of SF</i> Dark Era! Will write them in spare time as part of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges\"><b>WtA Tribes as WtF Lodges</b></a> project then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-22-2018, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T00:48:47-07:00","id":1256653,"title":"","content":"<b>Desert Wolf:</b> Desert wolf hunts the spaces between. He hunts the things that creep in through the cracks of the world, like Djinn and certain non-beings. It was one of the primary forces that fought the Idigam and helped Luna seal them on herself.<br /> <br /> Desert wolf was almost killed in that conflict and woke trapped in the Gauntlet. He was trapped for generations before he finally figured out where he was and how to navigate it. Now he can navigate between interstices and can cross almost any barriers imaginable when hunting his prey. A particularly disturbing trick is when he folds into the edges of a corner where the various planes meet. Much like some of the evil spirits he hunts, Desert Wolf can go to another realm that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mist Wolf:</b> Mist wolf hunts from ambush. She hides her movement in mists and rain and obscures her trail. She's not the most sneaky or deadly, but she certainly is effective. Her abilities aid her allies immensely. Calling up clouds to shade or rains and mists to obscure assist the entire pack.Mist Wolf is a mystical wolf that doesn't control weather, per se, but rather moves along with the fates that guide it. She has long since learned to duck into other realms to outmaneuver opponents and to hunt other game. It's said she has wooden claws but iron teeth. There's debate on how literally one should interpret that.<br /> <br /> Her hunt takes her into cities and tamed lands, but she's only ever able to rest in truly wild places. Lucky for her, there are still dreams about such things she can resort to. Her den is a cave in a glen deep in the Sacred Dream.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sea Wolf:</b> Sea Wolf isn't obviously Ur-Farah's child to modern eyes. His skin is grey and hairless. (Usually light grey, though it shifts quite a bit.) He has a long, sleek body designed for swimming and fins instead of paws and a tail instead of haunches. Packs of Sea Wolf Brothers take down sharks and other predators that would enter the world and bring bloody chaos.<br /> <br /> Sea Wolf can enter the Hisil by leaping out of the water or by splashing back into it. When the tribal totems were hunted, he was hunting the oceans, ignored. Mostly, he's been continuing his hunt with his Sea Wolf Brothers, unless there is some Tribe of Dolphin shifters that he patronizes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 09-23-2018, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T00:27:49-07:00","id":1257511,"title":"","content":"Awhile back, I toyed with an idea of alternative Forsaken Tribes myself, and I came up with the following Firstborn:<br /> <br /> Burning Wolf: Firstborn totem of the Hell-Eaters, Uratha who hunt down Wound-born spirits and servants of the Maeljin- particularly Bale Hounds.<br /> <br /> Grey Wolf: Firstborn totem of the Mist Seekers, a tribe who hunt ghosts and search out ancient secrets of Pangea and Uratha long gone <br /> <br /> Fangs-Incribed, or Geas Wolf: Firstborn totem of the Auger Kings, a Forsaken tribe who has discovered how to forcibly restore the Auspices of Uratha who have removed them. They hunt the Anshega and seek to unify the People under a single banner.<br /> <br /> Grinding Wolf: Firstborn totem of the Glass Breakers, a tribe dedicated in ensuring that humanity\u2019s progress does not outstrip its ability to control its creations, so they hunt powerful spirits tied to human born concepts as well as, rumored, the God-Machine\u2019s angels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T00:38:54-07:00","id":1257513,"title":"","content":"Awhile back, I toyed with an idea of alternative Forsaken Tribes myself, and I came up with the following Firstborn:<br /> <br /> Burning Wolf: Firstborn totem of the Hell-Eaters, Uratha who hunt down Wound-born spirits and servants of the Maeljin- particularly Bale Hounds.<br /> <br /> Grey Wolf: Firstborn totem of the Mist Seekers, a tribe who hunt ghosts and search out ancient secrets of Pangea and Uratha long gone <br /> <br /> Fangs-Incribed, or Geas Wolf: Firstborn totem of the Auger Kings, a Forsaken tribe who has discovered how to forcibly restore the Auspices of Uratha who have removed them. They hunt the Anshega and seek to unify the People under a single banner.<br /> <br /> Grinding Wolf: Firstborn totem of the Shepards of Glass, a tribe dedicated in ensuring that humanity\u2019s progress does not outstrip its ability to control its creations, so they hunt powerful spirits tied to human born concepts as well as, rumored, the God-Machine\u2019s angels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 09-27-2018, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T01:19:49-07:00","id":1258841,"title":"","content":"Riffing a little: Grey Wolf could focus on scent as a link to things of the past or hidden. Camo could be another sort of thing such a totem might provide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T03:40:03-07:00","id":1258848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1258841#post1258841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Riffing a little: Grey Wolf could focus on scent as a link to things of the past or hidden. Camo could be another sort of thing such a totem might provide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or an ability to pierce obfuscations and other illusions, both are equally fitting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T12:49:03-07:00","id":1258933,"title":"","content":"True enough. Similar enough to fit as facets of the same gift. Playing a bit with that notion, in fact.<br /> <br /> Current sketch:<br /> <br /> Cunning: Danger sense, while active, provides protection against most attacks via slight prescience.<br /> Glory: Call up shades of heroes past.<br /> Honor: Part the mists to allow allies to step in and walk them.<br /> Purity: Smell the past and track with the best conditions available within its window. Temporal manipulations stand out to the sense if they affect the window smelled. (from present back)<br /> (ed: Heck, it occurs to me that even just knowing the order scents were lain would be amazingly useful.)<br /> Wisdom: Visions of the past can reveal important events in the location.<br /> <br /> Most of these interact with the mists. While inside, Cunning allows sight of the &quot;present&quot;. Purity allows tracking through the mists to a specific target vista from which an event can be viewed. Vistas are significant events in time. Trails in the mists are mostly links of consequence connecting event to event. Wisdom can reveal vast details from vistas and share these with the pack.<br /> <br /> It would take some serious thinking and polishing to get right, but I likes it, I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-06-2018, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T14:56:56-07:00","id":1259665,"title":"","content":"Trolling back into this thread I have an... idea? Thought? This is going to get me into trouble....<br /> <br /> So Father/Mother Wolf had a variety of children. Malleable, semi-spirit children. Who's to say they all came out wolves? <br /> <br /> Maybe the secret to finally unraveling the &quot;other changing-breeds for WtF 2e&quot; is just -- they are all technically wolves and choose to affect a different form and mannerisms, because they can?<br /> <br /> From that perspective, anything that is half-human and half-spirit is a descendant of Wolf, even if they don't assume the precise form expected. Were-tigers? Wolves. Were-ravens? Wolves. Were-sharks? Wolves.<br /> <br /> &lt;ducks&gt;<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T09:30:28-08:00","id":1278090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1259665#post1259665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trolling back into this thread I have an... idea? Thought? This is going to get me into trouble....<br /> <br /> So Father/Mother Wolf had a variety of children. Malleable, semi-spirit children. Who's to say they all came out wolves? <br /> <br /> Maybe the secret to finally unraveling the &quot;other changing-breeds for WtF 2e&quot; is just -- they are all technically wolves and choose to affect a different form and mannerisms, because they can?<br /> <br /> From that perspective, anything that is half-human and half-spirit is a descendant of Wolf, even if they don't assume the precise form expected. Were-tigers? Wolves. Were-ravens? Wolves. Were-sharks? Wolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>There might be more to this idea than you think, Khanwulf.<br /> <br /> Urfarah was a Wolf, but he was the Pangean pillar that represented Hunting along with Boundaries, so theoretically all kinds of predatory shifters could of been born from Her union with Father Moon, though wolves would be far more likely to emerge.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the Necro, I remembered a couple more of those alternative Firstborn I had, which I will reveal next response lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T09:46:01-08:00","id":1278093,"title":"","content":"And as promised, two more that I remembered!<br /> <br /> Blind Wolf: The Firstborn Totem of the Pure Tribe known as the Maimed, a tribe fully comprised of former Forsaken elders who had been deposed, but not killed, by their younger contemporaries, and believe they understand the true error the Forsaken made by killing Mother Wolf through surviving such power plays. Thus they seek to find a way to revive Urfarah and ensure he never falls into decline again- primarily through the ritual sacrifice of the blood and Essence of the Urdaga.<br /> <br /> Lone Wolf: An unaffiliated Firstborn recently reawakened who seeks to create a Tribe of her own, but is unable to approach werewolves directly unless sought out first. So she sends omens and prophetic dreams to Ghosf Wolves, hoping they will find her and help build a Tribe together: a Sovereign Tribe that stands apart from Pure or Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 01-02-2019, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T14:12:52-08:00","id":1278150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1278090#post1278090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There might be more to this idea than you think, Khanwulf.<br /> <br /> Urfarah was a Wolf, but he was the Pangean pillar that represented Hunting along with Boundaries, so theoretically all kinds of predatory shifters could of been born from Her union with Father Moon, though wolves would be far more likely to emerge.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the Necro, I remembered a couple more of those alternative Firstborn I had, which I will reveal next response lol</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well... three months is hardly a necro; I don't think it dropped off the first page even!<br /> <br /> But yes, that was the bolt of realization: mother wolf's children don't have to be wolves, per se, they just have to be <b><i>related.</i></b> Even if they as a group have forgotten the face of their Father.<br /> <br /> By the same token, Luna's children don't have to be wolves, either. They're just likely to be <i>similar </i>to the wolves because Luna likes wolves. A lot. Too much, probably. Ehem.<br /> <br /> In the meantime I've been knocking around thoughts about what happens if Luna forces a change that doesn't... somehow hook into Wolf well enough. So the poor fool ends up maybe 3/4ths spirit because Luna forces the issue, figuratively or literally. A labor of love, so to speak<br /> <br /> In both these cases other werewolves would likely consider the results to be some kind of weirdness that needs hunting, or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lone Wolf: An unaffiliated Firstborn recently reawakened who seeks to create a Tribe of her own, but is unable to approach werewolves directly unless sought out first. So she sends omens and prophetic dreams to Ghost Wolves, hoping they will find her and help build a Tribe together: a Sovereign Tribe that stands apart from Pure or Forsaken. </div> </div> </div>Ooo! Let me play!<br /> <br /> And--and the first Ghost Wolf who joined is called &quot;Cub&quot;. Together they seek to avenge the death of Father Wolf by tracking down the <b><i>true</i></b> instigators of his demise! They're not sure, really, what that means--except, apparently, there will be ninjas!<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T09:42:02-08:00","id":1278340,"title":"","content":"That does make a lot of sense Khanwulf, it would make an interesting plot hook for sure!<br /> <br /> And wolf ninjas would be funny, though I\u2019m thinking it would probably be a bit more circumspect in that regard.<br /> <br /> Damn it I thought of a couple more Firstborn.. I\u2019ll post them in a bit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T09:59:05-08:00","id":1278345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1278340#post1278340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does make a lot of sense Khanwulf, it would make an interesting plot hook for sure!<br /> <br /> And wolf ninjas would be funny, though I\u2019m thinking it would probably be a bit more circumspect in that regard.<br /> <br /> Damn it I thought of a couple more Firstborn.. I\u2019ll post them in a bit!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... to be quite honest ninjas is just an effort to drive the square peg of a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lone_Wolf_and_Cub\" target=\"_blank\">Lone Wolf and Cub</a> reference that much deeper.<br /> <br /> Pushcart as they roam the Hisil is optional.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T12:37:59-08:00","id":1278380,"title":"","content":"Ok, so out-of-the-box Firstborn, starting with:<br /> <br /> <b>King Lion:</b> an ancient Pangaean contemporary with Father Wolf, it is said that he rarely hunted himself but instead was brought trophies by his pride and court of other Pangaeans. Lion Clan storytellers will say a lot more--out of earshot of wolves--about how King Lion was given both his mane and rulership over all that the sun looked upon after his great roar terrified a massive spirit called Theia into coughing up the half-devoured sun. They also say Wolf was given her job by King Lion, to patrol the boundaries of His domain and keep His subjects in check. (Lion Clan storytellers work hard to stay away from wolves....) King Lion hasn't been seen since the Sundering, and the same storytellers may--in exchange for satisfying their curiosity somehow, admit that King Lion himself said that like the sun, his rule would set.<br /> <br /> <b>Khan Tiger:</b> sometimes to King Lion's court would stalk the Lord of the East, Tiger. Tiger whispered that he was sovereign over all the jungle, where the sun could not see and Lion could not rule. But in truth the court knew that it was Lion's own claw that inscribed the symbol for &quot;king&quot; upon Tiger's forehead and granted him the dark jungles. For King Lion was wise in his rulership and recognized that bravery and power needed exercise, lest it turn against authority.<br /> <br /> <b>Mad Lord Jaguar:</b> Jaguar followed in Tiger's pawsteps and was once king of the jungles of the west, feared for his roar and mighty bite. But his behavior was erratic and terrifying to his subjects and he lost his crown. It is said that to this day the jaguar spirits are irrationally elusive, violent and vindictive. Even Jaguar Clan members hope that their forefather is as lost as the hunter's paradise he once stalked.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>Intermission:</b> I will now bestow a story I've told to my own kits several times. (IRL)<br /> <br /> <b>Mad Lord Jaguar</b><br /> <br /> Mad Lord Jaguar was king of the jungle!<br /> <br /> All of Mad Lord Jaguar\u2019s subjects lived in fear of him.<br /> <br /> He would do the strangest things:<br /> <br /> He called for them to fetch all the turtle shells in the jungle!<br /> <br /> And then showed off his strong teeth by biting them.<br /> <br /> (The turtles found still in their shells crawled away to the river while he was busy.)<br /> <br /> He would pretend to be a butterfly.<br /> <br /> And show off his jumping by going from flower to flower.<br /> <br /> (Neither the flowers nor the butterflies appreciated being landed on.)<br /> <br /> He liked to see himself in the river.<br /> <br /> So he had all his subjects carve his face into the jungle.<br /> <br /> The trees looked like Mad Lord Jaguar.<br /> <br /> The rocks looked like Mad Lord Jaguar.<br /> <br /> There were silly faces. (8*)<br /> <br /> There were fierce faces! (&gt;8x)<br /> <br /> There were serious faces. (8|)<br /> <br /> There were faces of Mad Lord Jaguar everywhere!<br /> <br /> The animals of the jungle called Lord Jaguar <i>mad</i>.<br /> <br /> It was crazy what he made them do! They had had enough!<br /> <br /> The animals of the jungle gathered to decide what should be done.<br /> <br /> Turtle said they would build big shells and hide in them?<br /> <br /> No\u2014 Lord Jaguar could turn them over and bite through them!<br /> <br /> Monkey said they would climb above the clouds and get away from him?<br /> <br /> No\u2014 Lord Jaguar would climb after them, and jump from tree to tree until they tired!<br /> <br /> Crocodile was not worried, they would swim into the river and wait?<br /> <br /> No\u2014 Lord Jaguar would swim like a fish and find them!<br /> <br /> Bird said they would fly away to other lands?<br /> <br /> No\u2014 Lord Jaguar would wait, and when they returned, he would be there!<br /> <br /> Prince Caracal lay in the sun, watching them all, and said nothing.<br /> <br /> Tapir was last to speak; he was slow, but had an idea: make a big face of their Lord, to honor him, and surprise him!<br /> <br /> All the animals grumbled, for this would mean extra work and they did not think anything would help.<br /> <br /> But they admitted it might put Lord Jaguar into a better mood.<br /> <br /> Finally the day for the celebration came--the unveiling of the Big Face.<br /> <br /> The animals called to Lord Jaguar, who stopped jumping on flowers to see what was going on.<br /> <br /> They pulled the leaves from the Big Face, and it looked just like an angry Lord Jaguar!<br /> <br /> From its mouth\u2014like a cave\u2014tapir gave his best roar, and it echoed across the jungle!<br /> <br /> Mad Lord Jaguar was so scared that he ran away, and his crown rolled off and fell into the river!<br /> <br /> And that is how Mad Lord Jaguar lost his crown; and Jaguar became no longer King of the Jungle!<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> <b>End Intermission.</b> Your regularly scheduled Wolf programming may resume.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 01-03-2019, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T13:00:56-08:00","id":1278386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a>, am I getting it right - Mother Wolf was only one of MANY Lords of Boundaries and Hunt, and King Lion, Khan Tiger and Mad Lord Jaguar are her <i>equals</i> - or different <i>emanations</i> of the same Pangean? I.E. Are they all Royal Avatars of the same being?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T13:28:29-08:00","id":1278398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1190942-of-firstborns-less-told-brainstorming?p=1278386#post1278386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a>, am I getting it right - Mother Wolf was only one of MANY Lords of Boundaries and Hunt, and King Lion, Khan Tiger and Mad Lord Jaguar are her <i>equals</i> - or different <i>emanations</i> of the same Pangean? I.E. Are they all Royal Avatars of the same being?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would entirely depend on whom you ask.<br /> <br /> I mean that quite literally.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> My intent for ... a few years now... has been to come to a plausible re-visioning of at least the Bastet from Changing Breeds. For 2e. To do that you need a mythology or <b>several</b>, vague enough that it can be interpreted as needed from different perspectives. So if you ask a Lion-Clan shape-changer they tell you all about how great their dude is/was. If you ask wolves they'll say these guys smell like weird wolves who got too close to cats or lions or whatnot, and muse about hunting them.<br /> <br /> So basically there can be a whole constellation of predatory animal-shifters who quite purposefully avoid wolves because they are presently the big dogs. And act like A-holes. Spirits are their allies in more of the way that they are to the Pure, because it's the forsaken in particular who've taken up Father Wolf's boundary policing obligations. So spirits are less likely to rat out other shifters and may have a web of ancient promises and obligations to fall back on.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the <i>Cat Must Know</i>.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T16:06:41-08:00","id":1284598,"title":"","content":"I have several more for you guys from this alternate reality Tribe project of mine ( which one day may be fleshed out like my Fang-Shapers.. in the next five to six fucking years xD)<br /> <br /> \u2014\u2014-<br /> Forsaken Totems:<br /> <br /> Gazing Wolf- The Tribal Totem of the Dream Wardens Tribe, Lucid Wolf\u2019s chosen hunt the most elusive and possibly most dangerous game: those entities that prey upon the mind and manipulate dreams. Spirits of dreams, Mastigos Mages, Changelings, Beasts- whatever creature that tampers with the sleeping mind is fair game.<br /> <br /> Luna is the font of prophecy through dreams, the agendas of lesser creatures pollute and undermine her dominion. <br /> <br /> More Flesh minded or compassionate Uratha hunt these things due to a desire to protect those they love from such parasitism.<br /> <br /> <br /> Restless Wolf- the tribal Totem for the Border Howlers Tribe, those who serve Restless Wolf are perhaps the most dedicated to honoring Urfarah out of all the Forsaken, as their Totem has taken the stability of the Gauntlet to be her utmost responsibility.<br /> <br /> Any who violate or cross the Gauntlet ( barring other Forsaken, usually) are the Sacred Prey of the Tribe, and they have a reputation of pursuing such offenders quite rabidly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Pure Totems:<br /> <br /> Chaser of Rain, or Squall Wolf- The tribal Totem of the Storm Riders Tribe, the faithful of Squall Wolf are in many ways the antithesis to the Border Howlers, as they wish to do away with the Gauntlet, in fact they wish to destroy anything and everything that would serve to constrain the Shadow . They worship the chaotic nature of the Hisil, and despise the stagnant, decaying structure of the human dominated physical world, and wish merge the two realms again in order to \u201c fix\u201d the world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}